          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did kiṇṇam mean, and what did peṭṭi mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கழுத்து",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கழுத்து (kaḻuttu) — \"the neck\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Malayalam കഴുത്ത് (kaḻuttŭ) is the same word, ழ and all — that letter again, the one only these two sisters still write. Telugu went its own way here, to మెడ (meḍa)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is the neck outside and the throat inside, both in one word. A garland goes round the கழுத்து (kaḻuttu), and so does the thread tied at a wedding."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கழுத்து (kaḻuttu) is native Dravidian. DEDR 1366 lists Malayalam kaḻuttu and Kannada kattu."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five more pieces of you."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
